  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between us: Contemporary Performing Arts project in Minya, Upper Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between Us is an 18-month contemporary performing arts project implemented by Dawar Arts in Minya Governorate, Upper Egypt, addressing structural gaps in artistic production, leadership, and access to culture outside Cairo. The project works with 75 young artists (aged 18&#x2013;35) organized into six independent theatre teams, resulting in the creation of seven original contemporary performances. It combines training, artistic residencies, production, touring, and international exchange into one integrated process. Four performances are developed through the translation and dramaturgical adaptation of contemporary Dutch theatrical texts, two performances draw on local heritage and contemporary lived narratives, and one Egyptian Dutch bilingual duo-drama is co-created by Egyptian and Dutch artists and performed in Arabic and Dutch on stage.  Performances are presented through a touring model across Minya&#x2019;s cities and villages, alongside selected presentations in Cairo, reaching an estimated 4,000&#x2013;5,000 audience members, many of them first-time theatre attendees.</narrative>
  </description>
